  "text": "umably, this question is referring to a trapezoid with two bases of 16 cm and 20 cm, and a height of h cm. When the trapezoid is rotated around its height, it forms a right circular cone with a volume of $1632\\pi \\;\\textrm{ cm}^3$. When the trapezoid is rotated around one of its bases, it forms a solid composed of two right circular cones sharing the same base and axis, with a volume of $960\\pi \\;\\textrm{ cm}^3$.\n\nTo find the height of the trapezoid, we can start by finding the radius of the circular base formed by rotating the trapezoid around its height. This radius is equal to the length of the shorter base of the trapezoid, which is 16 cm.\n\nNow, we can use the volume formula for a cone, which is given by:\n\nVolume = (1/3) * π * r^2 * h\n\nwhere r is the radius of the circular base and h is the height of the cone.\n\nFor the first part of the question, when the trapezoid is rotated around its height, it forms a right circular cone with a volume of $1632\\pi \\;\\textrm{ cm}^3$. Plugging in the values, we get:\n\n$1632\\pi = (1/3) * π * 16^2 * h$\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n$1632 = (1/3) * 256 * h$\n\n$1632 = 85.33 * h$\n\nDividing both sides by 85.33, we get:\n\n$h = 19.12$ cm\n\nSo, the height of the trapezoid is approximately 19.12 cm.\n\nTo verify this answer, we can plug it back into the volume formula for the cone and check if it matches the given volume of $1632\\pi \\;\\textrm{ cm}^3$.\n\nFor the second part of the question, when the trapezoid is rotated around one of its bases, it forms a solid composed of two right circular cones sharing the same base and axis. The volume of this solid is $960\\pi \\;\\textrm{ cm}^3$. Using the same volume formula for a cone, we can plug in the values and solve for the height of the cones.\n\n$960\\pi = (1/3) * π * 16^2 * h$\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n$960 = (1/3) * 256 * h$\n\n$960 = 85.33 * h$\n\nDividing both sides by 85.33, we get:\n\n$h = 11.31$ cm\n\nSo, the height of each cone formed when the trapezoid is rotated around one of its bases is approximately 11.31 cm.\n\nTherefore, the height of the trapezoid is approximately 19.12 cm.",
